# The guest follows the host's log, mends the lost seq 3 with a snapshot (seq 4 is in it;
# whole once its shown characters and map state and HP parts came), starts over at the wipe's new
# epoch, drops the old log's late frame and forgets the log when it leaves.
world log path: log (1 peer has it)
wlog member follows epoch 5a1700000001
wlog member applied seq 1 reset every map
wlog member applied seq 2 kill 0x10014066 on 0x18010000
wlog member gap: has seq 2, host at 4
wlog member gap: has seq 2, host at 4
wlog member gap: has seq 2, host at 4
wlog member gap: has seq 2, host at 4
wlog member snapshot to seq 4
wlog member shown on 0x0: 0 characters
wlog member map state of 0x0
life wipe
wlog member follows epoch 5a1700000002
wlog member applied seq 1 reset every map
wlog member applied seq 2 kill 0x1001400a on 0x18010000
wlog member dropped an older log's frame
wlog member applied seq 3 unkill 0x1001400a on 0x18010000
life leave
wlog member reset
world log path: board (no peers)
